      "side": 1,
      "message": "Jerome, Marco: To avoid unnecessary complexity to support scenarios our clients don\u0027t need, I suggest we consider requiring libvpx clients to destroy the encoder after `vp9_change_config()` fails with `VPX_CODEC_MEM_ERROR`. Then we have a simpler goal: make it safe to call `vpx_codec_destroy()` in this case.",
      "revId": "ec14ef65fd342af1f1ef24d926c413a6e117d600",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
