      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T17:44:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A data point for that: with only the parent change (8571539), vpx_codec_destroy() is already safe after this failure; ConfigResizeAllocFailureVp9 checks it. A client that keeps the encoder instead can crash: on i386 with ASan, 64x64 -\u003e 46340x46340 (VPX_CODEC_MEM_ERROR) -\u003e vpx_codec_enc_config_set() back to 64x64 writes through NULL in vp9_enc_setup_mi() (vp9_change_config -\u003e update_frame_size -\u003e vp9_init_context_buffers). So with that requirement, the encoder would still need to refuse its other calls after the error to keep a client that misses it safe.\n\nThis CL refuses encode and the controls that use these buffers while realloc_pending is set, and lets a later config_set retry the reallocation.",
      "parentUuid": "f32d9f87_afa25c7b",
